From d636c2a24c41c3c87f7222b9eb1971c94979f247 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yann Gautier <yann.gautier@st.com>
Date: Tue, 21 Apr 2026 18:53:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 506/572] fix(st-pmic): stub some functions for
 STM32MP_STPMIC1L

If STM32MP_STPMIC1L is enable, we use the STPMIC2 driver, with STPMIC1
include file. And the functions print_pmic_info_and_debug() and
pmic_voltages_init() do nothing in that case. Instead of defining them
in STPMIC2 driver, stub them in STPMIC1 include file under the flag
STM32MP_STPMIC1L.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/arm-trusted-firmware.git 789677eeb0e6e2c00c4bf3eec5a4c48a83f44e85 fix(st-pmic): stub some functions for STM32MP_STPMIC1L]
Change-Id: I503327daa5098c99c48bbd78fb2253cebfbf390b
Signed-off-by: Yann Gautier <yann.gautier@st.com>
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/st/tf-a/+/572146
Reviewed-by: Maxime MERE <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
Tested-by: Yann GAUTIER <yann.gautier@foss.st.com>
